UID:70rjco9o6sq64b9m6cq64b9k75i3gbb2c4qm4b9g70rm8or16cqj2c9h70@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260515T052337Z
DESCRIPTION:Jazz on a Summer’s Day/Festival i Jazz\, Yhdysvallat 1959 
 • O: Bert Stern\, Aram Avakian • Thelonious Monk\, Anita O’Day\, Chu
 ck Berry\, Chico Hamilton\, Louis Armstrong\, Mahalia Jackson • restauro
 itu versio • DCP • S • 82 min • näytöksen alustaa laulaja Anna I
 nginmaa\n\nKesä\, merellinen ympäristö ja jazz\, voisiko parempaa toivo
 a! Newportin jazzfestivaalin 1958 hienossa taltioinnissa mukana ovat muun 
 muassa Thelonious Monk\, Jimmy Giuffre\, Sonny Stitt\, Anita O'Day\, Dinah
  Washington\, Gerry Mulligan\, Chico Hamilton\, Louis Armstrong ja Mahalia
  Jackson. Kun lisäksi saamme näytökseemme upeasti restauroidun kopion\,
  ei tätä tunnelmapalaa kannata jättää väliin! \n\nIlmainen.\n\nToine
 n näytös pe 7.8. klo 17.15.\n\nKino Regina juhlistaa Jazz Suomi 100 -juh
 lavuotta jazzelokuvien sarjalla\, jossa näytösten alustajiksi on kutsutt
 u kotimaisia eturivin jazzmuusikoita. Koko kesäohjelmisto julkaistaan 9.6
 . Lisätietoja näytöksistä osoitteessa kinoregina.fi.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260515T055712Z
LOCATION:Kino Regina\, Töölönlahdenkatu 4\, 00100 Helsinki\, Suomi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Something Else vol. 15 | Pérez Nagano / Sofia / Peña
DTSTART:20260625T160000Z
DTEND:20260625T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260621T125905Z
UID:6hhm4c9o70pm6b9m6sr3gb9k6oq38b9ocgqjgbb46hj6acpg6or36c9o68@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260603T094159Z
DESCRIPTION:Folk\, experimental\, classical\, contemporary\, and a cross-A
 tlantic meeting of musicians and multidisciplinary performers originally f
 rom Mexico now residing in Helsinki - Something Else v15 brings together f
 lutist/electronic musician Kenji Pérez Nagano and cellist Victoria Sofia\
 , guest-hosted and -curated this June by poet\, translator\, and transmedi
 a artist Amado Peña.\n\nSuggested donation €10-25 (mobilepay or cash)\n
 2 sets\n\nSOMETHING ELSE is a concert series for improvised music focused 
 on new meetings of musicians from across Helsinki's free improv\, experime
 ntal\, jazz\, electronic\, and global music scenes\, hosted on the 4th Thu
 rsday of each month at Kallio's Musta Kissa bar. New small-ensemble groupi
 ngs - often first-time meetings - are highlighted each time\, with an emph
 asis on surprise\, difference\, curiosity\, energy\, and connection.\n\nKE
 NJI PÉREZ NAGANO is a Mexican musician and electronic music producer. His
  primary instruments are Transversal Flute and Bansuri (Indian Flute). Whi
 le drawing influences from Folk music from Latin America\, and Indian clas
 sical music he started his carrier as an electronic music producer in Berl
 in where he studied sound design in Psychedelic and Techno. Recently he is
  part of Jaranas del Norte in Finland\, in collaboration with K'u'um Colle
 ctive promoting Son Jarocho (Mexican Folk) as a Jaranero and singer.\nhttp
 s://www.instagram.com/ecayari\n\nVICTORIA SOFIA is a Helsinki-based cellis
 t and multidisciplinary musician from Mexico working across classical musi
 c\, traditional genres\, and contemporary expression through collaborative
  performance. Her artistic practice focuses on creative experimentation\, 
 and shared musical experiences.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/victoriaorsofia
 \n\nAMADO PEÑA is a poet\, translator\, and transmedia artist. With a bac
 kground in Hispanic Language and Literature and specializations in Cultura
 l Management\, and Mexican Literature in Indigenous Languages\, his practi
 ce unfolds across writing\, performance\, and material experimentation.\nh
 ttps://www.instagram.com/pancakesinpijamas/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260603T094600Z
LOCATION:Musta Kissa Bar\, Toinen linja 15\, 00530 Helsinki\, Suomi
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-JAZZFI-SOURCE:gcal
END:VEVENT
